# Dropdown / listbox standard

Use the shared Expense Ledger–style listbox for all product dropdowns.

## Required stack

- Markup: `templates/partials/ep_form_listbox_macros.html` (`ep_listbox` / `ep_toolbar_listbox`) or the same `data-se-listbox` chip structure
- Behavior: `static/ep_form_listbox.js` (`initEpListboxes`, `resetEpListbox`)
- Styles: `static/ep_form_listbox.css` (CSS variables `--ep-listbox-*`)

## Do

- Prefer listbox chips over native `<select>` in UI forms, filters, and panels
- Keep a hidden `<input>` for the selected value; update display via `resetEpListbox(fieldId, value, label)`
- Include `ep_form_listbox.css` + `ep_form_listbox.js` on any page that adds a new listbox
- Reuse existing classes: `ep-form-listbox`, `ep-toolbar-listbox`, `ep-combobox-listbox`

## Don't

- Don't invent a new dropdown visual (custom menus, Bootstrap selects, one-off panels)
- Don't restyle open menus in page CSS unless layout requires it (width, z-index, clipping)
- Don't use native `<select>` for branded product UI

## Visual tokens (source of truth)

Open panel: light blue border (`--ep-listbox-panel-border`), soft shadow, 12px radius, 6px padding.
Options: 8px radius; selected/hover blue tint (`--ep-listbox-selected-bg` / `--ep-listbox-selected-fg`).
